{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"increased-hardshell-cougar","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe advisory dogfood proves the project criterion can execute and retain its identity through the four-pass Gerrit review pipeline. One FIRE control is not enough evidence to enable blocking or change the 0.90 threshold.\n\n## Plan\n- Accumulate a representative set of real advisory review outcomes over time.\n- Measure priority distribution, false positives, abstentions, and author impact.\n- Propose any threshold or blocking_enabled change with data and a separate Gerrit review.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The evidence set and sampling window are documented.\n- [ ] Promotion or continued advisory-only posture is justified from measured outcomes.\n- [ ] Any routing change lands through an independently reviewed ticket and Gerrit change.\n\nOut of scope for the current dogfood session.","id":"4f40-ed2f-94bf-419a","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["review-architecture","project-criteria","calibration"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Evaluate blocking posture for project.review-phase-boundaries from production review data"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785215887912141001,"uuid":"f539b6e8-f3f6-4264-af4b-13208e5a067d"}